teria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/scripts/reclaim_bridge_history.py implements export_and_import (fast-export|fast-import streaming), _commit_metadata (author/committer/parent/message parse), restore_current_bridge_state (commit-tree replay preserving author/committer/message/parents), _copy_data_block, is_partial_clone refusal, protected_remote_refs snapshot, and assert_rewrite invariant checks","infra/scripts/reclaim_comment_echo_history.py already imports and reuses ReclaimError, _copy_data_block, ref_exists, ref_name, rev_parse, run_git from reclaim_bridge_history — establishing an intra-repo reuse pattern for these primitives","The plan's step 2 ('replays retained commits above the boundary with preserved author/committer/message/timestamps and rewritten parent marks') restates functionality already present in _commit_metadata + restore_current_bridge_state","These scripts target DIFFERENT payloads (Jira bridge caches / comment-echo), so this is a rebuild-vs-extend ambiguity, not a proven straight duplication"],"finding":"The plan proposes a new git fast-import + commit-tree rewrite engine without acknowledging the existing core-git rewrite primitives in infra/scripts/reclaim_bridge_history.py and infra/scripts/reclaim_comment_echo_history.py, several of whose helpers are directly reusable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5a9fa2362e80f2be","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1-2 (rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse fast-import stream)","norm_id":"n22e24f702de25058","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The implementer re-derives fast-export/fast-import streaming, commit-metadata parsing, commit-tree replay, and clone-safety refusals from scratch, diverging from (and possibly regressing behind) the hardened infra/scripts logic (e.g. partial/promisor-clone refusal, binary data-block framing)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"