w/bdf3-.../...json' checklist_item flags 'the ordering/fixpoint discipline that keeps ledger position.commit_sha consistent with the FINALIZED rewritten graph'."],"finding":"Step 3's ledger re-resolution has an unstated ordering/fixpoint hazard: `build_position_commit_map` resolves each retained event's `position->commit_sha` from the committed rewritten graph, but the SNAPSHOT tree that STORES those resolved commit_shas is itself part of that graph. Emitting the updated ledger tree through fast-import mints a new commit (and can shift descendant SHAs), which may invalidate the commit_sha values just written for retained in-horizon commits. The plan asserts the re-resolution + re-emission happens but does not specify the ordering that makes the resolved map consistent with the FINALIZED graph.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffa84ab1e1aa4efb9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan, step 3 ('use `authorship_resolution.build_position_commit_map` against the rewritten graph ... Emit the updated tree through fast-import')","norm_id":"ncb28a81334b2b80c","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Re-emitting the SNAPSHOT tree with resolved commit_shas produces a new commit whose descendants' SHAs differ from what build_position_commit_map saw, leaving stale/dangling commit_sha annotations for retained in-horizon events.","verify-authorship then re-resolves a position to a commit that the finalized branch no longer carries at that SHA."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachab